# Spring Boot Zero Day Remediation Playbook

## 1. Purpose

Remediate all Spring Boot and Spring Framework components flagged in a Zero Day
event by upgrading each artifact to its approved version as listed in the PAA
Spring Framework Versions sheet, validating via Black Duck scan, and completing
the OSS validation process.

Scope is strictly limited to Spring dependency version changes. No other code,
logic, configuration, or dependency is touched unless it directly blocks the
Spring upgrade and the human explicitly approves it.

> **Non-negotiable principle**: Make only the version changes that Black Duck
> and the PAA Spring Framework Versions sheet require. Match each artifact ID
> to its approved version exactly. Never change application behavior, public
> contracts, security configuration, logging, telemetry, business logic, or
> test expectations unless the change is required for Spring remediation AND
> the human explicitly approves it. This will not be a one-time event — every
> change must be clean, minimal, and repeatable.

-----

## 2. Scope

**Applies to** Java/Kotlin applications containing one or more of:

- `spring-boot-starter-*` in any version
- `org.springframework.*` direct dependencies or BOM imports
- `spring-security-*` dependencies
- `spring-cloud-*` dependencies
- `spring-data-*` dependencies
- `spring-batch-*` dependencies
- `spring-integration-*` dependencies
- Orchestra Spring Boot wrapper (`orchestra-spring-boot-*`)

**In scope — version strings only:**

- `pom.xml` (root and all module files)
- `build.gradle`, `build.gradle.kts`
- `gradle.properties`
- `gradle/libs.versions.toml`
- `settings.gradle`, `settings.gradle.kts` (if they declare plugin versions)
- Explicit `<properties>` overrides for Spring artifacts
- Explicit `ext {}` / `dependencyResolutionManagement` overrides for Spring
  artifacts

**Out of scope — never touch without explicit human approval:**

- Any `.java` or `.kt` source file
- Any test source file
- `application.yml` / `application.properties` / `bootstrap.yml`
- Non-Spring dependencies of any kind
- Dockerfile, CI/CD pipeline, Kubernetes or Helm manifests
- Database migration scripts
- `pom.xml` structure, formatting, element ordering, or non-version fields
- Architecture, module structure, or dependency graph shape

> If the approved version, artifact ID, current version string, or build file
> structure is ambiguous — stop and ask one precise question before proceeding.

-----

## 3. Repository Discovery

Execute fully before editing any file. Do not skip steps.

### 3.1 Build System Identification

- Determine if the project uses Maven, Gradle, or both
- For Maven: locate all `pom.xml` files including submodules referenced in
  `<modules>`
- For Gradle: locate `build.gradle` or `build.gradle.kts`, `settings.gradle`
  or `settings.gradle.kts`, `gradle.properties`, and
  `gradle/libs.versions.toml` if present
- Determine if the project is single-module or multi-module

### 3.2 Spring Version Inventory

Identify and record:

- Current Spring Boot version — source: `<parent>` block,
  `spring-boot-starter-parent`, BOM import, or `springBootVersion` property
- Current Spring Framework version if overridden separately
- Current Spring Cloud BOM version if present
- Current Spring Security version if overridden separately
- Current Spring Data BOM version if overridden separately
- Current Orchestra wrapper version if present
- Every Spring artifact declared with an explicit version — record artifact ID,
  current version string, file, and line number
- Every Spring artifact declared without a version (BOM-managed) — record
  artifact ID and note as BOM-managed
- The exact version string format in use for each artifact:
  - Numeric: `3.2.4`
  - Release train: `2.1.8.RELEASE`
  - Milestone: `4.0.0-M1`
  - Snapshot: `3.5.0-SNAPSHOT`

### 3.3 Black Duck Scan Inventory

If a Black Duck scan report is provided:

- Extract every flagged Spring component: artifact ID, current version, CVE IDs
- Record each as a remediation target
- Cross-reference against the Spring version inventory from 3.2

### 3.4 Discovery Output

Before making any change, present the inventory to the human as:

```
DISCOVERY SUMMARY
=================
Build system: Maven | Gradle | Both
Project structure: Single-module | Multi-module (N modules)
Spring Boot version: X.X.X (source: <file>)
Spring Cloud BOM: X.X.X | NOT PRESENT (source: <file>)
Orchestra wrapper: X.X.X | NOT PRESENT

EXPLICIT SPRING VERSION OVERRIDES FOUND:
- <artifact-id>: <version> (<file>:<line>)

BOM-MANAGED SPRING ARTIFACTS (no explicit version):
- <artifact-id>

BLACK DUCK FLAGGED COMPONENTS:
- <artifact-id>: <version> (CVE-XXXX-XXXXX, ...)

SNAPSHOT VERSIONS FOUND (will not be changed):
- <artifact-id>: <version> (<file>)
```

