## 4. PAA Spring Framework Versions Sheet — Lookup Rules

The PAA Spring Framework Versions sheet (`All PAA Apps_Spring Rajeev List` tab)
is the authoritative source of approved versions. The `Pivot` tab is for
summary only — do not use it for version resolution.

**Columns used:** `Artifact ID`, `Component Version Name` (approved version),
`Project`, `Publicly Accessible`.

**Lookup procedure:**

1. For each Spring artifact in the repository, look up its `Artifact ID` in
   the sheet
1. `Component Version Name` is the approved target version
1. If the same artifact ID appears in the sheet with different versions across
   rows, select the version that matches the project’s current Spring Boot major
   line — 2.x uses Framework 5.x versions, 3.x uses Framework 6.x versions,
   4.x uses Framework 7.x versions — do not mix lines
1. If the artifact ID is not in the sheet, do not change its version — flag as
   NOT FOUND IN SHEET in the remediation report
1. If the `Project` column on the sheet row matches the current repository name,
   that row takes precedence over a generic row for the same artifact ID

