## 5. Version String Format Rules

### 5.1 Standard Numeric (e.g., 3.2.4, 6.2.17)

Use the version string exactly as shown in the sheet. No suffix, no qualifier.

### 5.2 Release Train Format (e.g., 2.1.8.RELEASE)

Legacy Spring Data format used before calendar versioning.

- If the repo has `2.1.8.RELEASE` and the only sheet-approved version for that
  artifact is in the 3.x line (e.g., `3.2.4`), this is a major version jump —
  stop, report as BLOCKER, ask human for explicit approval before proceeding
- If the sheet lists `2.1.8.RELEASE` as the approved version, use that exact
  string including `.RELEASE` — do not normalize it

### 5.3 Milestone Format (e.g., 4.0.0-M1)

Pre-release version.

- Apply only if it is the only approved version in the sheet for that artifact
  in the 4.x line
- If the project is on Boot 3.x and the only sheet entry for an artifact is a
  milestone, do not apply it — flag as LINE MISMATCH — NOT APPLIED
- Never substitute a milestone with a GA version or vice versa

### 5.4 Snapshot Format (e.g., 3.5.0-SNAPSHOT)

- Never change a SNAPSHOT version — flag it in the report as SNAPSHOT —
  NOT CHANGED and ask the human whether to address it

-----

## 6. Version Resolution by Spring Boot Major Version

Apply exactly one upgrade path based on the current Spring Boot major version.
Do not mix paths. Do not cross a major version boundary without explicit human
approval.

### 6.1 Spring Boot 4.x / Spring Framework 7.x

- Use the PAA sheet approved version for each artifact in the 4.x line
- `4.0.0-M1` milestone versions apply per Section 5.3
- Orchestra wrapper: `4.1.5`
- Spring Cloud: use the approved Spring Cloud 2024.x BOM version if listed in
  the sheet; if not listed, stop and ask — do not guess
- Java: 17 or higher required — if below 17, stop and report BLOCKER
- Tomcat: 11.x required — if below 11, stop and report BLOCKER

### 6.2 Spring Boot 3.x / Spring Framework 6.x

- Use the PAA sheet approved version for each artifact in the 3.x line
- `spring-aop`: `6.2.15`
- `spring-data-keyvalue`: `3.2.4`, or `3.4.4` if project is already on 3.4.x
- `spring-data-redis`: `3.2.4`
- `spring-security-oauth2-client`, `spring-security-oauth2-core`,
  `spring-security-crypto`: `6.5.9` — update as explicit overrides
- `spring-jcl`, `spring-tx`, `spring-webflux`: `6.2.17`
- Orchestra wrapper: `3.23.8`
- Spring Cloud: use the approved Spring Cloud 2023.x BOM version if listed in
  the sheet; if not listed, stop and ask — do not guess
- Do not upgrade from 3.x to 4.x — requires separate human-approved migration
- Java: 17 or higher required — if below 17, stop and report BLOCKER
- Tomcat: 10.x required — if below 10, stop and report BLOCKER

### 6.3 Spring Boot 2.x / Spring Framework 5.x

- No major version upgrade in this 72-hour window
- `spring-aop`: `5.3.29` — update only if explicitly overridden in build files
- `spring-beans`: `2.7.14` — update only if explicitly overridden
- `spring-data-redis` at `2.1.8.RELEASE` with sheet 3.x version `3.2.4`:
  major jump — stop, flag as BLOCKER, ask human
- Apply only approved patch versions for 2.x artifacts listed in the sheet;
  if no 2.x patch version is listed, make no change to that artifact
- Spring Cloud: use the approved Spring Cloud 2021.x BOM version if listed in
  the sheet; if not listed, stop and ask — do not guess
- Post-event: document a migration plan to Boot 3.x or 4.x in the report —
  do not execute it
- Boot 2.x is approaching end-of-life — record as risk item

### 6.4 Java and Tomcat

- Not required for this event unless they directly block the Spring upgrade
- If upgrade is needed to unblock Spring, stop and ask for explicit approval

