## 16. Stop Conditions

Stop immediately and ask the human one precise question if any of the following
are true. Do not proceed. Do not guess.

- The PAA Spring Framework Versions sheet is not provided and the approved
  version for a specific artifact cannot be determined from the table in
  Section 4
- The current Spring Boot major version cannot be identified from build files
- Java is below 17 and the target is Spring Boot 3.x or 4.x
- Tomcat is below 10 and the target is Spring Boot 3.x, or below 11 for 4.x
- An artifact is at `2.1.8.RELEASE` and the only PAA sheet version is in the
  3.x line — major jump requires explicit human approval
- The same artifact ID appears in the sheet with versions from two different
  major lines and the project’s target line is ambiguous
- Spring Cloud is present but no approved Spring Cloud BOM version is in the
  PAA sheet
- A child module independently declares a Spring version override that conflicts
  with the root upgrade
- A flagged Black Duck artifact is not in the PAA sheet and has no obvious
  Spring owner
- Any `application.yml` or `application.properties` key must change due to a
  removed or renamed property in the target Spring version
- The build file structure is non-standard and the authoritative Spring version
  declaration cannot be identified without ambiguity
- More than one Spring Boot major version is present across modules
- A SNAPSHOT version of a Spring artifact is present and it is unclear whether
  it should be replaced
- An Orchestra wrapper version conflict is detected per Section 10

