## 17. Principles Summary

- Match every artifact ID to its PAA sheet approved version — no guessing,
  no inferring
- Preserve the exact version string format shown in the PAA sheet
- Never apply a milestone version unless it is the only sheet-approved version
  for that artifact in the project’s major line
- Never cross a major version boundary without explicit human approval
- Never change application code, tests, config files, or unrelated dependencies
- Handle Spring Cloud BOM separately — never assume a compatible version
- Detect and report Orchestra wrapper transitive conflicts before marking
  complete
- Never change SNAPSHOT versions without human instruction
- Always produce a full remediation report with per-artifact detail
- OSS validation is part of remediation — it is not complete until the
  re-scan is clean
- This will not be a one-time event — every change must be clean, minimal,
  reviewable, and repeatable
